Subject: [PATCH] ANSI prototypes in wait.c/ilmid.c, flex %option, cleanups

Split out of the same warning sweep because these are different concerns from
the const-correctness work in 706.

* Two K&R definitions converted to ANSI prototypes: ilmid/wait.c's AsnOctsCopy
  and ilmid/ilmid.c's compare_attachment_point. ttcp.c's eleven are in 706,
  which owns that file. Parameter types are copied verbatim from the old-style
  declaration run, so the compiled code is unchanged; both
  -Wold-style-definition and -Wstrict-prototypes go away.

* ilmid/wait.c reset_remsys(): two statements had lost their newline, so
  `if (x) free(x);        if (y) free(y);` and
  `if (x) free(x);        memset(...)` read as if the trailing statement were
  guarded by the preceding if. It is not, and it must not be - the memset has to
  run on every call. One statement per line now; behaviour unchanged and
  -Wmisleading-indentation is gone.

* src/mpoad/io.c: include <poll.h> rather than <sys/poll.h>. musl answers the old
  form with `#warning redirecting incorrect #include <sys/poll.h> to <poll.h>`,
  and the redirect target is exactly what we were already getting.

* The four flex scanners (qgen/ql_l.l, test/ispl_l.l, sigd/cfg_l.l,
  switch/cfg_l.l) get `%option nounput noinput`. Nothing in this package calls
  yyunput() or input(), so suppressing their emission removes 8
  -Wunused-function warnings.

  Only the .l sources are patched, deliberately. The generated .c files ship in
  the tarball but are rebuilt during the package build - automake's .l.c suffix
  rule runs whenever the .l is newer, and applying this very patch is what makes
  it newer. They are also already machine-dependent in practice: the shipped
  src/qgen/ql_l.c is 1894 lines in the tarball but comes out 1907 lines on this
  build host, so a diff against any one build's copy would be wrong on another's.

* src/sigd/cfg_y.y: hex2num() is a static helper in the yacc prologue with no
  caller anywhere in the tree. Same reasoning as above about not touching the
  generated cfg_y.c.
--- a/src/ilmid/wait.c
